WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.361
Step six reads the service
principal sign-ins over an

2
00:00:03.361 --> 00:00:07.425
eighteen-day window and summarizes
them, principal by principal.

3
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:13.162
Ring 1 is ready for enforcement: Mail
Automation and Payroll Export are both clear.

4
00:00:13.162 --> 00:00:14.537
Ring 2 isn't ready.

5
00:00:14.537 --> 00:00:18.295
Deploy Bot would be blocked,
because it signed in from two oh

6
00:00:18.295 --> 00:00:22.437
three dot oh dot one thirteen dot
seven, outside the egress ranges.

7
00:00:22.437 --> 00:00:26.863
And HR Connector has no sign-ins at
all, so there's nothing to judge.

8
00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:30.575
A ring is ready only when
every principal in it is clear.

9
00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:32.600
The summary ends with its hash.

10
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.861
Write that hash down: in step eight,
the enforcement record cites it,

11
00:00:36.861 --> 00:00:41.260
and that's how a reviewer's approval
is tied to exactly this evidence.
